-- secure_random_bytes
32 bytes arrived: true
and there are 32 of them: true
every one is a byte: true
they are not all the same value: true
a second call gives different bytes: true
-- past the 256-byte cap
1,000 bytes arrived, all 1,000: true
every one is a byte: true
the four blocks are not the same block: true
at least 200 of the 256 byte values appear in 1,000 draws: true
-- secure_random_int_below
every roll is 0 to 5: true
each of the six faces lands 10000 +/- 500: true
below(1) is always 0: true
-- secure_uuid_v4
36 characters, hyphens at 8 13 18 23: true
the version nibble is always 4: true
the variant nibble is always 8, 9, a or b: true
all four variant values appear in 200 draws: true
everything else is a lowercase hex digit: true
two calls differ: true
-- tokens
32 bytes of hex is 64 characters: true
and every one is a lowercase hex digit: true
32 bytes of unpadded base64url is 43 characters: true
and nothing in it needs escaping in a URL: true
-- a real key through lib/encoding.bx
a 32-byte key survives base64 and back: true
and hex and back: true
-- string_equals_constant_time
equal strings: true
differing in the FIRST byte: true
differing in the LAST byte: true
differing in the middle: true
a prefix is not the whole: true
and the whole is not a prefix: true
empty against empty: true
empty against something: true
something against empty: true
a repeat of the shorter is still not equal: true
nor is a triple: true
two strings that differ only after a NUL: true
and the same one twice: true
-- bytes_equals_constant_time
a key against itself: true
a key against another: true
empty against empty: true
empty against one byte: true
one byte against empty: true
